#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform in an organization"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangan untuk menyediakan IBM Quantum Platform dalam sesebuah "
"organisasi"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform for an organization"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangan untuk menyediakan IBM Quantum Platform bagi sesebuah organisasi"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore chemlab */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore chemlab */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Considerations for setting up IBM Quantum Platform for an organization "
"{#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangan untuk menyediakan IBM Quantum Platform bagi sesebuah organisasi"
" {#considerations-for-setting-up-ibm-quantum-platform-for-an-organization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In an organization where individuals might work on several projects, IBM "
"Quantum Platform governance can seem complex. However, access management can"
" be used to easily enable user collaboration and to restrict visibility of "
"users and projects when necessary. Managing access becomes more relevant "
"with IBM Quantum Platform resources that are not free - that is, service "
"instances that use paid plans (which organizations are charged for).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam sesebuah organisasi di mana individu mungkin mengerjakan beberapa "
"projek, tadbir urus IBM Quantum Platform boleh kelihatan kompleks. Walau "
"bagaimanapun, pengurusan akses boleh digunakan untuk memudahkan kerjasama "
"pengguna dan menyekat keterlihatan pengguna dan projek apabila perlu. "
"Pengurusan akses menjadi lebih relevan dengan sumber IBM Quantum Platform "
"yang tidak percuma — iaitu, instans perkhidmatan yang menggunakan pelan "
"berbayar (yang dikenakan bayaran kepada organisasi).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"overview-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   IBM Cloud&reg; provides various ways to implement these mechanisms described in this guide. There are several ways to achieve these objectives. Additionally, most of the steps in this guide are generic to IBM Cloud and not specific to IBM Quantum Platform, except the custom role details.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   IBM Cloud&reg; menyediakan pelbagai cara untuk melaksanakan mekanisme yang diterangkan dalam panduan ini. Terdapat beberapa cara untuk mencapai objektif ini. Selain itu, kebanyakan langkah dalam panduan ini adalah generik kepada IBM Cloud dan tidak khusus untuk IBM Quantum Platform, kecuali butiran peranan tersuai.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Involved personas {#involved-personas}"
msgstr "Persona yang terlibat {#involved-personas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The are several main personas that are mentioned in this guide:\n"
msgstr "Terdapat beberapa persona utama yang disebutkan dalam panduan ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**User**: Someone who gets access to IBM Quantum Platform resources "
"(_service instances_) and can potentially collaborate with other users on "
"these resources. Users' access is controlled by an administrator and they "
"cannot create or delete service instances.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pengguna**: Seseorang yang mendapat akses kepada sumber IBM Quantum "
"Platform (_instans perkhidmatan_) dan berpotensi bekerjasama dengan pengguna"
" lain pada sumber tersebut. Akses pengguna dikawal oleh pentadbir dan mereka"
" tidak boleh membuat atau memadam instans perkhidmatan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Cloud administrator**: An IBM Cloud account owner who owns IBM Quantum "
"Platform resources and manages which users can access these resources. As "
"the resource owner, the administrator is charged for any paid resource "
"use.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pentadbir Cloud**: Pemilik akaun IBM Cloud yang memiliki sumber IBM "
"Quantum Platform dan menguruskan pengguna yang boleh mengakses sumber "
"tersebut. Sebagai pemilik sumber, pentadbir dikenakan bayaran untuk sebarang"
" penggunaan sumber berbayar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**IDP administrator**: An administrator who defines identities and their "
"attributes in an identity provider (IDP).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pentadbir IDP**: Pentadbir yang menentukan identiti dan atributnya dalam "
"pembekal identiti (IDP).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Terminology {#terminology}"
msgstr "Terminologi {#terminology}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This guide uses the following terms:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menggunakan istilah berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Resource_: A generic IBM Cloud term that refers to an object that can be "
"managed through the Cloud user interface, CLI, or API. For this guide, a "
"_resource_ is an IBM Quantum Platform service instance.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Sumber_: Istilah generik IBM Cloud yang merujuk kepada objek yang boleh "
"diuruskan melalui antara muka pengguna Cloud, CLI, atau API. Untuk panduan "
"ini, _sumber_ ialah instans perkhidmatan IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Service instance_: A service instance is used to access Cloud services - "
"specifically, quantum computers. It is defined through the catalog. You can "
"define several service instances based on the same or different plans, which"
" offer access to different quantum computing backends. See [Available IBM "
"Cloud plan](/guides/plans-overview) for details.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Instans perkhidmatan_: Instans perkhidmatan digunakan untuk mengakses "
"perkhidmatan Cloud — khususnya, komputer kuantum. Ia ditakrifkan melalui "
"katalog. Anda boleh menentukan beberapa instans perkhidmatan berdasarkan "
"pelan yang sama atau berbeza, yang menawarkan akses kepada Backend "
"pengkomputeran kuantum yang berbeza. Lihat [Pelan IBM Cloud "
"tersedia](/guides/plans-overview) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Project_: A grouping unit that enables users to work on the same resources."
" This guide uses two projects: `ml` and `finance`. See [Hierarchical project"
" structures](#nest-org) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Projek_: Unit pengelompokan yang membolehkan pengguna bekerja pada sumber "
"yang sama. Panduan ini menggunakan dua projek: `ml` dan `finance`. Lihat "
"[Struktur projek hierarki](#nest-org) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      This project is not related to the \"project\" concept in the classic IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"      Projek ini tidak berkaitan dengan konsep \"projek\" dalam IBM Quantum&reg; Platform klasik.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"xplanning-orgx\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Plan your setup {#plan-your-setup}"
msgstr "Rancang persediaan anda {#plan-your-setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you set up IBM Quantum Platform for your organization, you need to "
"make these decisions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum anda menyediakan IBM Quantum Platform untuk organisasi anda, anda "
"perlu membuat keputusan ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How are user identities defined? You can set up IBM Cloud users, users from "
"another identity provider (IDP), or both.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimanakah identiti pengguna ditakrifkan? Anda boleh menyediakan pengguna "
"IBM Cloud, pengguna daripada pembekal identiti lain (IDP), atau kedua-"
"duanya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are using a different IDP, does the Cloud administrator or the IDP "
"administrator assign users to project resources?\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika anda menggunakan IDP yang berbeza, adakah pentadbir Cloud atau "
"pentadbir IDP yang menugaskan pengguna kepada sumber projek?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the IDP administrator assigns users to projects, you need a string to be "
"used as a key, such as `project` (which this guide uses) for project "
"comparisons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika pentadbir IDP menugaskan pengguna kepada projek, anda memerlukan "
"rentetan untuk digunakan sebagai kunci, seperti `project` (yang digunakan "
"panduan ini) untuk perbandingan projek.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What are the projects and which service instances will belong to each? You "
"must plan your project names carefully.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apakah projek-projek tersebut dan instans perkhidmatan mana yang akan "
"tergolong dalam setiap projek? Anda mesti merancang nama projek anda dengan "
"teliti.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do not make project names substrings of another. For example, if you use "
"`ml` and `chemlab` for project names, then later you set up a project match "
"for `ml`, it triggers on both values, accidentally granting more access than"
" expected. Instead, use unique names such as `ml` and `chem-lab`. "
"Alternatively, use prefix or suffix values to avoid such unintended "
"substring matches.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jangan jadikan nama projek sebagai subrentetan bagi projek lain. Contohnya, "
"jika anda menggunakan `ml` dan `chemlab` sebagai nama projek, kemudian anda "
"menyediakan padanan projek untuk `ml`, ia akan mencetuskan pada kedua-dua "
"nilai, secara tidak sengaja memberikan lebih banyak akses daripada yang "
"dijangkakan. Sebaliknya, gunakan nama unik seperti `ml` dan `chem-lab`. "
"Sebagai alternatif, gunakan nilai awalan atau akhiran untuk mengelakkan "
"padanan subrentetan yang tidak disengajakan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using naming conventions along with prefix or suffix values can help you "
"easily allow access to several projects.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan konvensyen penamaan bersama dengan nilai awalan atau akhiran "
"boleh membantu anda membenarkan akses kepada beberapa projek dengan mudah.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum experiments (jobs) belong to service instances, and users that have "
"access to an instance can see its jobs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen kuantum (kerja) tergolong dalam instans perkhidmatan, dan "
"pengguna yang mempunyai akses kepada instans tersebut boleh melihat "
"kerjanya.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Service instances can be based on different plans, allowing access to "
"different backends.\n"
msgstr ""
"Instans perkhidmatan boleh berdasarkan pelan yang berbeza, membenarkan akses"
" kepada Backend yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Which users need to access which projects?\n"
msgstr "Pengguna mana yang perlu mengakses projek mana?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Should users be able to delete jobs? Keeping jobs in service instances gives"
" more traceability for billing costs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlukah pengguna boleh memadam kerja? Menyimpan kerja dalam instans "
"perkhidmatan memberikan lebih kebolehkesanan untuk kos bil.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Will you use access groups that directly reference IBM Quantum Platform "
"service instances or organize services into resource groups?\n"
msgstr ""
"Adakah anda akan menggunakan kumpulan akses yang merujuk terus kepada "
"instans perkhidmatan IBM Quantum Platform atau mengatur perkhidmatan ke "
"dalam kumpulan sumber?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Access groups** are a convenient and common way of controlling user access"
" for IBM Cloud resources. They are a simple but powerful means to "
"consistently assign user access. We create an access group for each project "
"and map users to access groups. Each access group uses a custom role that "
"allows users to access specific service instances or resource groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kumpulan akses** ialah cara yang mudah dan biasa untuk mengawal akses "
"pengguna bagi sumber IBM Cloud. Ia merupakan cara yang mudah tetapi berkuasa"
" untuk memberikan akses pengguna secara konsisten. Kami membuat kumpulan "
"akses untuk setiap projek dan memetakan pengguna kepada kumpulan akses. "
"Setiap kumpulan akses menggunakan peranan tersuai yang membolehkan pengguna "
"mengakses instans perkhidmatan atau kumpulan sumber tertentu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Resource groups** are used only when you need to maintain a clear "
"separation of service instances. If more service instances are created in a "
"resource group, all users that have access to the resource group see them "
"automatically without updating access groups. If you choose to use resource "
"groups, you will create access groups and then assign them to resource "
"groups.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kumpulan sumber** digunakan hanya apabila anda perlu mengekalkan pemisahan"
" jelas instans perkhidmatan. Jika lebih banyak instans perkhidmatan dibuat "
"dalam kumpulan sumber, semua pengguna yang mempunyai akses kepada kumpulan "
"sumber akan melihatnya secara automatik tanpa mengemas kini kumpulan akses. "
"Jika anda memilih untuk menggunakan kumpulan sumber, anda akan membuat "
"kumpulan akses dan kemudian menugaskannya kepada kumpulan sumber.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   A service instance can belong to only one resource group. After instances are assigned into resource groups, they cannot be changed. This also means that the resource group assignment can  happen only at service instance creation. Therefore, resource groups might not provide enough flexibility if assignments of service instances to resource groups might need to change.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Instans perkhidmatan hanya boleh tergolong dalam satu kumpulan sumber. Setelah instans ditugaskan ke dalam kumpulan sumber, ia tidak boleh diubah. Ini juga bermakna penugasan kumpulan sumber hanya boleh berlaku semasa penciptaan instans perkhidmatan. Oleh itu, kumpulan sumber mungkin tidak memberikan fleksibiliti yang mencukupi jika penugasan instans perkhidmatan kepada kumpulan sumber perlu berubah.\n"
"   </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Considerations {#considerations}"
msgstr "Pertimbangan {#considerations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should understand the following considerations when setting up your "
"environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda perlu memahami pertimbangan berikut apabila menyediakan persekitaran "
"anda.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define more fine-grained roles {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"
msgstr ""
"Takrifkan peranan yang lebih terperinci {#define-more-fine-grained-roles}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The actions in the custom roles can be used for more fine-grained access "
"control. For example, some users might need full access to work on service "
"instances, while others might only need Read access to service instances, "
"programs, and jobs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tindakan dalam peranan tersuai boleh digunakan untuk kawalan akses yang "
"lebih terperinci. Contohnya, sesetengah pengguna mungkin memerlukan akses "
"penuh untuk bekerja pada instans perkhidmatan, manakala yang lain mungkin "
"hanya memerlukan akses Baca kepada instans perkhidmatan, program, dan "
"kerja.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve that, define two different custom roles, such as `MLreader` and "
"`MLwriter`. Remove all cancel, delete, and update roles from the `MLreader` "
"custom role, and include all actions in the `MLwriter` custom role. Next, "
"add the roles to two different access groups accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mencapai itu, takrifkan dua peranan tersuai yang berbeza, seperti "
"`MLreader` dan `MLwriter`. Alih keluar semua peranan batal, padam, dan kemas"
" kini daripada peranan tersuai `MLreader`, dan sertakan semua tindakan dalam"
" peranan tersuai `MLwriter`. Seterusnya, tambah peranan kepada dua kumpulan "
"akses yang berbeza mengikutnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When using dynamic rules, that is, when the identity provider (IDP) administrator manages access through custom IDP user attributes, do not use IDP custom user attributes that are substrings of each other. For instance, don't use `ml` and `mlReader`, as the string comparison of `ml` would also accept `mlReader`. You could use `MLreader` and `MLwriter` to avoid this conflict.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Apabila menggunakan peraturan dinamik, iaitu apabila pentadbir pembekal identiti (IDP) menguruskan akses melalui atribut pengguna IDP tersuai, jangan gunakan atribut pengguna tersuai IDP yang merupakan subrentetan antara satu sama lain. Contohnya, jangan gunakan `ml` dan `mlReader`, kerana perbandingan rentetan `ml` juga akan menerima `mlReader`. Anda boleh menggunakan `MLreader` dan `MLwriter` untuk mengelakkan konflik ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an example of setting up custom roles, see [Create access groups for "
"projects](/guides/custom-roles).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk contoh menyediakan peranan tersuai, lihat [Buat kumpulan akses untuk "
"projek](/guides/custom-roles).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"shared-access\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shared workload access {#shared-workload-access}"
msgstr "Akses beban kerja dikongsi {#shared-workload-access}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is important to note that access applies to service instances.  Thus, "
"users with 'write' access to an instance can cancel their own workloads, but"
" can also view and cancel other users' workloads.  This is a function of how"
" IAM works and cannot be changed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk diingat bahawa akses terpakai kepada instans perkhidmatan. "
"Oleh itu, pengguna yang mempunyai akses 'tulis' kepada instans boleh "
"membatalkan beban kerja mereka sendiri, tetapi juga boleh melihat dan "
"membatalkan beban kerja pengguna lain. Ini adalah fungsi cara IAM berfungsi "
"dan tidak boleh diubah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"other-cloud-rsc-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"other-cloud-rsc-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Cloud resources {#other-cloud-resources}"
msgstr "Sumber Cloud lain {#other-cloud-resources}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The steps in this guide can be used to manage access to other Cloud "
"resources as well. Include the appropriate permissions to the access groups "
"of the relevant projects.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah-langkah dalam panduan ini boleh digunakan untuk menguruskan akses "
"kepada sumber Cloud lain juga. Sertakan kebenaran yang sesuai kepada "
"kumpulan akses projek yang berkaitan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"nest-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hierarchical project structures {#hierarchical-project-structures}"
msgstr "Struktur projek hierarki {#hierarchical-project-structures}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this guide, the mapping of users to projects and service instances was "
"kept simple. However, by associating several users with access groups and "
"referencing service instances from several access groups, more complex "
"mappings can be implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam panduan ini, pemetaan pengguna kepada projek dan instans perkhidmatan "
"dibuat mudah. Walau bagaimanapun, dengan mengaitkan beberapa pengguna dengan"
" kumpulan akses dan merujuk instans perkhidmatan dari beberapa kumpulan "
"akses, pemetaan yang lebih kompleks boleh dilaksanakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This method can accommodate a hierarchical structure. That is, it can align "
"to how users might be assigned to the Hub/Group/Project access structure in "
"the classic version of IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. For example, a _group_ "
"could be an access group that is assigned to all service instances of the "
"group's projects. Users who should get access to all of the group's projects"
" would then only have to be added to the group's access group.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaedah ini boleh menampung struktur hierarki. Iaitu, ia boleh diselaraskan "
"dengan cara pengguna mungkin ditugaskan kepada struktur akses "
"Hub/Kumpulan/Projek dalam versi klasik IBM Quantum&reg; Platform. Contohnya,"
" sebuah _kumpulan_ boleh menjadi kumpulan akses yang ditugaskan kepada semua"
" instans perkhidmatan projek kumpulan tersebut. Pengguna yang sepatutnya "
"mendapat akses kepada semua projek kumpulan kemudiannya hanya perlu ditambah"
" kepada kumpulan akses kumpulan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"repeat-org\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consistent and repeatable deployment of the configuration {#consistent-and-"
"repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"
msgstr ""
"Penggunaan konfigurasi yang konsisten dan boleh diulang {#consistent-and-"
"repeatable-deployment-of-the-configuration}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The steps of this guide can be automated for consistent and repeatable "
"management of users, projects, and the mapping between those. Refer to the "
"[Terraform IBM Cloud&reg; Provider "
"documentation](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-"
"Cloud/ibm/latest/docs) for templates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah-langkah panduan ini boleh diotomatikkan untuk pengurusan pengguna, "
"projek, dan pemetaan antara keduanya yang konsisten dan boleh diulang. Rujuk"
" [dokumentasi Pembekal IBM Cloud&reg; "
"Terraform](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/IBM-"
"Cloud/ibm/latest/docs) untuk templat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use Terraform to set allocation and limits, as well as restrict "
"backend access for `quantum-computing` service instances. See the [Getting "
"started with Terraform on IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-cloud-"
"provider-for-terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-"
"started) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh menggunakan Terraform untuk menetapkan peruntukan dan had, serta "
"menyekat akses backend untuk instans perkhidmatan `quantum-computing`. Lihat"
" [Memulakan dengan Terraform pada IBM Cloud](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/ibm-"
"cloud-provider-for-terraform?topic=ibm-cloud-provider-for-terraform-getting-"
"started) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

